from the beginning:
Me and my pal Cujo, still a puppy, begin our descent,
killing everything in sight. Cujo takes maybe a quarter
 of the kills. Found some tripe fairly early, then found an
armor outlet around lvl 3, where Cujo stole some
gauntlets of power. Yes. Also found a nice plate mail,
and dipped myself an excalibur.

Continue down.. lose Cujo to a lvl teleport trap
somewhere in the mines above minetown, but luckily
he is found one floor down w/ the help of a
magic whistle.

His luck was not to last long.

In minetown, some good, some bad. Cujo stole back
my money from the General Store on a number of
occasions, as well as a ring of free action,
and TWO magic markers (one of which was
destined to be blown on ID scrolls).

Invested in some divine protection until i got annoyed
 with the process. Cujo is killed by guard captain
(i was to get revenge later). A bad unicorn was lurking
around, killed him for his ivory. Got a good bones thingy:
 cursed luckstone and cursed speedboots. Put on
the speedboots with plans to christen later,
sell the luckstone for later retrieval.

Tamed a large dog w/ a food ration at the near the
oracle. Christened him Cujo II. Finished up Sokoban
 without mishap. Got amulet of reflection and
much dinero. Got enlightened at T:9341, had basic
 valk intrinsics + ESP

On way back to the Mines I converted an altar and
sacrificed for Mojo. Got some holy water to fix my luckstone.

Decided to go ahead and clear out all the mines,
got the regular luckstone, and headed down to medusa.

along the way decided to rub my lamps. one was indeed
magical and netted me GDSM. Cujo II is lost to another
lvl teleport trap.

Found =oTC on MDlvl14, and then hunted leprachaun meat.
Went back to Minetown to pick up candles. Threw my Mojo
defending the general store only to have it land at my feet and
auto-forfeited (?!?!). Did the only sensible thing - fought my
way out committing murder upon murder (including the Watch
 Cap'n) until i realized i could just teleport back to the stairs...

Got to medusa, teleported onto her island. blinded self, but
that prolly wasn't necessary. The amulet did her in. broke
perseus, he had a sack which did not turn out to be a BoH.
Passed on the shield of reflection.

At the castle. played mastermind style w/ a bugle.. boy
were the soldiers pissed. Drawbridge comes down, and
a lith emerges. having read of the insane badness of liths
i zapped a wand of death at him (i think i got it in Soko).

Cleared the castle without incident, got my wand of wishing:
 BoH first off. Then 2 blessed ?oGeno for L's and h's (sorry
 Samwise). hit lvl 14. Hit the quest. Went without incident.
Sacrificed for Grayswaindir had lotsa cash on hand.. it
all went to the priest of Molloch. at this point had around
-41 AC (cloak of protection, GDSM, dwarvish helm, small
shield, hawaiian shirt, spd boots, gaunts of power all
enhanced to +4 or 5) was lvl 15, and had all the basic
resistances. decided i wanted an archon pal, and wished
for a blessed figurine. Named him Archie in a moment of
alliterated enlightenment. lost a level to a vamp., and
from then on used Excalibur against 'em.

Went into hell. Plowed a 1 deep path b/w up and down stairs.
Refused to pay off the big boys, and pulled the upstairs
gimmick. No real trouble until Orcus town.. where I met
Orcus, who introduced me to Yeenoghu. Killed Orcus in
his own house and chased Yeenoghu up one level. Killed him,
but not before being introduced to Demogorgon. Aha.. an even match.
Didn't wanna mess w/ cockatrices, so kept on applying my u-horn
and eventually managed to smite his ruin upon the mountain side (not
before losing Archie, however). Continue down Gehennom, making
occasional trips back to pay the priest in the Valley. Found a large
dog,
named him Cujo III. He became a hellhound at some point, and finally
lived up to his name.

Get the scare of my life in seeing Rodney while blind... then realize
he's sleeping and won't wake until i say so. Vlad's stairs are on the
same level. Lose another level to a vamp in a moment of
brain fart. Got the candlebraum, amulet of LS, drank a smoky
potion in a quick haste. Turned into a grey dragon... awesome.
Lose my cloak and shirt, but armor's *thankfully* ok. down to -35 AC
or so. Pray for help and am restored.

Continue down to vibrating square. Along the way Cujo III is greased
by an Ice Devil. Ah well. Engrave elbereth with /oFire on the Square,
leave bell and candles on square, at Maniac's suggestion.

Luckily, portal to Rodney's tower is only one floor up. On the
mezzanine, clear out the zoo but keep the (final) large dog.
Cujo IV at least survived.. maybe I planned to whistle him into \
Rodney's room, but a White Dragon kindly froze the moat for me.
Dug into the wall. Rodney starts a fight, but is shut up w/ a /oDeath.

Performed Invocation. Fought my way thru the crowd, used up the
Bell to find the secret door. Instakillled the High Priest. Dumped my
 gold to unburden. Took the amulet, and then a break in order to
 calm my nerves.

few hours later, began my ascent. Ran into Rodney 5 times in
Gehennom.. had maybe 4 strange sensations sending me back
down. No biggie, until i ran outta death rays. Only had one wish
left and no marker charges, so i decide to go toe to toe w/ old
Rodney. 1 lvl below Jubilex he clones himself. I terminate
him once and followed his shadow up. He put up little trouble
the second time.

The rest of the Ascent, bar some cursing, went smoothly.
At lvl 1 decided to wish for a magic marker. wrote charging for
death wand, wasted one on a cached marker.
Enchanted a new spankin cloak of invis. i forgot i
stashed, putting AC back up to 40. Took the reverse plunge...

Zapped Rodney to death, and cleared the immediate
area. An *insanely* close call when i tried to read his
spellbook of digging. It froze me and a vampire and
earth elemental go medieval on my @$$ for a good
many turns. HP about 60/190 (from 230/230) after the feast,
my lvl having been dropped to 15 (from 19) by the vamp.

I putz around on Plane of Earth for long while, when
I realize Orb of Fate can find the portal. (i neglected
to find any ?o gold detection or the like). Had plenty of
wands of digging (around 9 i believe) to facilitate.

Got tossed around a bunch in Plane of Air. Was hurtin'
but made my way to the portal with 60 HP left. Threw
on a ring of regen once i got to the fire. The Air elementals
must've hurt my intelligence pretty bad, coz i was down to
12. The Orb confused me many times before it worked.
Recharged it and went to the water.

Blinded self and nearly [expletived] a brick seeing all the
sea monsters. Wrote myself a genocide scroll and wiped
out ;'s. The Orb *thankfully* worked on the second try.
Hit the astral planes.

Went to the Middle shrine first. Instadeath'd Famine, and
*very* slowly plowed my way into the shrine. Durn near
sacrificed my amulet when i realized the High Priestess
was for Loki not Tyr. I cried a little, then plunged back out.
Ran into Famine again on the way to Right side. Instakilled
him. I dont know why but i didn't see Pestilence or Death
in the Right bubble... hrm... by now I had made it back up to
lvl 17 through prayer and lotsa killin'. Had sort of a close call
right before entry into the Right temple - a peaceful angel
of Tyr clogged up the intake. Eventually realized i could teleport
him and did, but not before getting lots of things thrown at me
outside. HP down to 140/209. Thank Tyr it was the correct
altar. I then reached immortality.

Now I can sleep, and see if my girlfriend will return my calls.

